'''''Supergirl''''' is an American [[Superhero fiction|superhero]] [[Drama (film and television)|drama]] television series developed by [[Ali Adler]], [[Greg Berlanti]] and [[Andrew Kreisberg]] that aired on [[CBS]] from October 26, 2015, to April 8, 2016, and [[The CW]] from October 10, 2016, to November 9, 2021. Based on the [[DC Comics]] [[Supergirl (Kara Zor-El)|character]] created by [[Otto Binder]] and [[Al Plastino]], the series follows [[Supergirl (Arrowverse)|Kara Zor-El]] (played by [[Melissa Benoist]]), [[Superman (Arrowverse)|Superman]]'s cousin, and one of the last surviving [[Kryptonian]]s from the planet [[Krypton (comics)|Krypton]]. As Supergirl, Kara uses her powers to protect National City. The series was retroactively incorporated into the [[Arrowverse]] beginning with its [[Supergirl season 2|second season]], and became definitively linked with the rest of the franchise in the [[Supergirl season 5|fifth season]].

The series was officially picked up on May 6, 2015, after receiving a full series commitment in September 2014. Following a full season order on November 30, 2015, it transitioned to The CW for its second season going forward.

''Supergirl'' received positive-to-mixed reviews from critics, with praise for its creative direction and cast performances (especially Benoist's), though its handling of [[Political fiction|political]] themes such as [[empowerment]] and [[social justice]] was criticized by some{{who|date=September 2026}} audiences. It won the [[Critics' Choice Television Award for Most Exciting New Series|Most Exciting New Series]] at the [[5th Critics' Choice Television Awards]] in 2015. The television series ''[[Superman & Lois]]'' was developed as a direct spin-off of ''Supergirl'' with [[Tyler Hoechlin]] and [[Elizabeth Tulloch]] reprising their Arrowverse roles; however, after [[COVID-19 restrictions]] led to a planned [[Superman & Lois season 1|first season]] crossover with ''Supergirl'' being cancelled, creative redevelopment led to the series being [[retcon]]ned as being set in its own continuity from its [[Superman & Lois season 2|second season]] onward, with no narrative ties to ''Supergirl'', rendering it a stand-alone spin-off.

==Series overview==
{{Main|List of Supergirl episodes}}
{{:List of Supergirl episodes}}
[[Supergirl (Arrowverse)|Kara Zor-El]] was sent to [[Earth]] from [[Krypton (comics)|Krypton]] as a 13-year-old by her parents, [[Zor-El]] and [[Alura (DC Comics)|Alura]]. Kara was tasked with protecting her infant cousin, [[Superman|Kal-El]], but her spacecraft was knocked off course and trapped in the [[Phantom Zone]] for 24 years. By the time her spacecraft crash-landed on Earth, Kal-El had already grown up and become [[Superman]]. The series begins 12 years later, with Kara embracing her superhuman powers and adopting the superhero alias "Supergirl".<ref name="DeadlineSep2014">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=September 19, 2014 |title='Supergirl' Drama From Greg Berlanti & Ali Adler Lands CBS Series Commitment |url=https://deadline.com/2014/09/supergirl-tv-series-cbs-dc-greg-berlati-ali-adler-836682/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140919200127/http://deadline.com/2014/09/supergirl-tv-series-cbs-dc-greg-berlati-ali-adler-836682/ |archive-date=September 19, 2014 |access-date=September 19, 2014 |website=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref>

'''Season 1'''

In [[Supergirl season 1|Season 1]], Kara reveals her powers to become National City's protector.<ref name="TVLineOct2014">{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=October 30, 2014 |title=Meet CBS's Supergirl (''and'' Her Sister), Get Scoop on Kara's Big Entrance |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/supergirl-tv-show-cbs-casting-560953/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141030214639/http://tvline.com/2014/10/30/supergirl-tv-show-cbs-casting/ |archive-date=October 30, 2014 |access-date=October 30, 2014 |website=TVLine}}</ref> She discovers that numerous criminals her mother imprisoned have escaped to Earth, including her aunt [[Astra (DC Comics)|Astra]] and her uncle [[Non (character)|Non]]. Kara works with her adoptive sister [[Alex Danvers]], the Green Martian [[Martian Manhunter|J'onn J'onzz]], [[Jimmy Olsen|James Olsen]], and tech genius Winn Schott to fight these threats.

'''Season 2'''

In [[Supergirl season 2|Season 2]], Kara and her allies face tensions between humans and extraterrestrials while investigating [[Project Cadmus]], run by Lillian Luthor, [[Lex Luthor]]'s mother. Kara befriends [[Lena Luthor]], Lillian's adoptive daughter, and navigates her romantic feelings for [[Lar Gand|Mon-El]], a prince from [[Daxam]], Krypton's neighboring planet. Meanwhile, James becomes the vigilante [[Guardian (DC Comics)|Guardian]], Alex begins dating [[Maggie Sawyer]], and J'onn forms a bond with [[Miss Martian|M'gann M'orzz]], a [[White Martian]].

'''Season 3'''

In [[Supergirl season 3|Season 3]], Kara grapples with Mon-El's departure, only for him to return from the 31st century, where he has founded the [[Legion of Super-Heroes|Legion]] and married [[Saturn Girl|Imra Ardeen]]. J'onn reunites with his father, [[M'yrnn J'onzz]], and Kara's new friend, Samantha Arias, unknowingly transforms into the world-killing weapon [[Reign (Arrowverse)|Reign]].

'''Season 4'''

In [[Supergirl season 4|Season 4]], Kara confronts rising anti-alien sentiments fueled by Lex Luthor, who manipulates [[Agent Liberty|Ben Lockwood]] into forming a human-first group, the Children of Liberty, forcing her to fight against prejudice and for the [[civil and political rights]] of aliens. Meanwhile, a Kara clone, dubbed [[Superman: Red Son|Red Daughter]], trains in [[Kasnia]] to fight Supergirl at Lex's request. Tensions arise as Col. Lauren Haley joins the DEO, demanding that Supergirl reveal her identity, which she refuses to do.

'''Season 5'''

In [[Supergirl season 5|Season 5]], Kara and her friends face a new threat, [[Leviathan (DC Comics)|Leviathan]], while adjusting to life on the newly created Earth-Prime following the [[Multiverse (DC Comics)|multiverse]]-altering [[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis]] on Infinite Earths. Kara also faces challenges working under Lex Luthor, as Leviathan continues their covert operations.

'''Season 6'''

In [[Supergirl season 6|Season 6]], the final season, Lex seeks to continue the Anti-Monitor's work by conquering the multiverse and imprisons Kara in the [[Phantom Zone]], where she discovers her father is also trapped. After being rescued, Kara and her team face the fifth-dimensional imp [[Ms. Gsptlsnz|Nyxlygsptlnz]], who escaped the Phantom Zone and seeks revenge on her father. Lex eventually allies with Nyxlygsptlnz, leading to the final showdown in the series.

