* [[Melissa Benoist]] as [[Kara Danvers|Kara Zor-El / Kara Danvers / Supergirl]]:  A [[Kryptonian]] living in National City, who must embrace her powers after previously hiding them. She assists her adoptive sister Alex as part of the [[Department of Extranormal Operations|Department of Extra-Normal Operations]] (DEO) as she discovered the truth that her adoptive father also worked for the DEO so they would not take her, while Alex's co-workers at the DEO help her perfect her powers.<ref name="DeadlineSep2014" /><ref name="BenoistCast">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=January 22, 2015 |title=Melissa Benoist Is Supergirl: CBS Pilot Casts 'Glee' Actress In Lead Role |url=https://deadline.com/2015/01/melissa-benoist-supergirl-cast-cbs-pilot-glee-1201355085/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150124042258/http://deadline.com/2015/01/melissa-benoist-supergirl-cast-cbs-pilot-glee-1201355085/ |archive-date=January 24, 2015 |access-date=January 22, 2015 |website=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref><ref name="S1Logline">{{Cite web |last=Goldman |first=Eric |date=May 13, 2015 |title=CBS Schedule: Supergirl Airing on Mondays; Person of Interest Held for Midseason |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/05/13/cbs-schedule-supergirl-airing-on-mondays-person-of-interest-held-for-midseason |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150516024742/http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/05/13/cbs-schedule-supergirl-airing-on-mondays-person-of-interest-held-for-midseason |archive-date=May 16, 2015 |access-date=May 13, 2015 |website=IGN}}</ref> Kara worked as [[Cat Grant]]'s assistant at CatCo.<ref name="SupportingCast">{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=October 31, 2014 |title=CBS' Supergirl Casting Jimmy Olsen, Cat Grant and Others |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/supergirl-casting-jimmy-olsen-cat-grant-561270/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151121050244/http://tvline.com/2014/10/31/supergirl-casting-jimmy-olsen-cat-grant/ |archive-date=November 21, 2015 |access-date=October 31, 2014 |website=TVLine}}</ref> Benoist expressed her excitement over portraying the character, and being able to "[tell] a story about a human being really realizing their potential and their strength".<ref name="CBRint">{{Cite web |last=Huver |first=Scott |date=February 25, 2015 |title=Melissa Benoist Embraces "Supergirl's" Iconic Qualities & Powerful Humanity |url=https://www.cbr.com/melissa-benoist-embraces-supergirls-iconic-qualities-powerful-humanity/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150226031531/http://www.comicbookresources.com/article/melissa-benoist-embraces-supergirls-iconic-qualities-powerful-humanity |archive-date=February 26, 2015 |access-date=February 25, 2015 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> [[Malina Weissman]] (seasons 1-2) and [[Izabela Vidovic]] (seasons 3-4 & 6) portray a young Kara.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=March 9, 2015 |title=CBS Casts Young 'Supergirl' (Exclusive) |url=https://hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cbs-casts-young-supergirl-779887 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150311145900/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cbs-casts-young-supergirl-779887 |archive-date=March 11, 2015 |access-date=March 9, 2015 |website=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref><ref name="YoungActors">{{Cite web |last=Swift |first=Andy |date=September 5, 2017 |title=Supergirl Recasts Two Key Roles |url=http://tvline.com/2017/09/05/supergirl-recast-young-kara-alex-season-3-spoilers/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170905185935/http://tvline.com/2017/09/05/supergirl-recast-young-kara-alex-season-3-spoilers/ |archive-date=September 5, 2017 |access-date=September 6, 2017 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>
* [[Mehcad Brooks]] as [[Jimmy Olsen|James "Jimmy" Olsen]] / [[Guardian (DC Comics)|Guardian]] (seasons 1–5; guest: season 6): A former ''[[Daily Planet]]'' photographer, James moved to National City and became the new [[art director]] for his former colleague, Cat Grant, at CatCo Worldwide Media. He is initially a potential love interest for Kara.<ref name="S1Logline" /><ref name="SupportingCast" /><ref name="BrooksCast">{{Cite web |last=Wagmeister |first=Elizabeth |date=January 28, 2015 |title=Mehcad Brooks Cast in CBS' 'Supergirl' as Melissa Benoist's Love Interest |url=https://variety.com/2015/tv/news/supergirl-mechad-brooks-cast-james-olsen-1201417912/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150201140824/http://variety.com/2015/tv/news/supergirl-mechad-brooks-cast-james-olsen-1201417912/ |archive-date=February 1, 2015 |access-date=January 28, 2015 |website=Variety}}</ref> Among his reasons for moving across the country are his breakup with his fiancée, Lucy Lane,<ref name="How Does She Do It?">{{Cite episode |title=How Does She Do It? |episode-link=#ep5 |series=Supergirl |last=Berlanti |first=Greg |author-link=Greg Berlanti |network=[[CBS]] |date=November 23, 2015 |season=1 |number=5 |author-link2=Ali Adler |first2=Ali |last2=Adler |author-link3=Andrew Kreisberg |first3=Andrew |last3=Kreisberg}}</ref> and keeping an eye on the newly revealed Supergirl for Superman. While working at the ''Daily Planet'', James received the [[Pulitzer Prize]] for taking the first photograph of Superman. In the second season, James becomes [[Guardian (DC Comics)|Guardian]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Swift |first=Andy |date=October 11, 2016 |title=Supergirl EP Reveals James' Future as DC Comics' Guardian, Explains Why He and Kara Are 'Best as Friends' |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/supergirl-spoilers-season-2-james-guardian-kara-relationship-757637/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161015133814/https://tvline.com/2016/10/11/supergirl-spoilers-season-2-james-guardian-kara-relationship/ |archive-date=October 15, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |website=TVLine}}</ref> In the fourth episode of season 5, James decides to leave National City to run his hometown newspaper. He returns in the series finale to assist the Superfriends in the final battle against Lex and Nyxly and attend Alex and Kelly's wedding.
* [[Chyler Leigh]] as [[Alex Danvers|Alexandra "Alex" Danvers / Sentinel]]: Kara's human adoptive sister. She is a physician, bioengineer, scientist and government agent who serves as Hank Henshaw's right hand at the DEO.<ref name="SupportingCast" /><ref name="LeighHarewoodKreisberg">{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=February 26, 2015 |title=CBS 'Supergirl' Enlists Chyler Leigh, David Harewood |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/supergirl-chyler-leigh-david-harewood-778058 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150227004531/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/supergirl-chyler-leigh-david-harewood-778058 |archive-date=February 27, 2015 |access-date=February 26, 2015 |website=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref><ref>{{Cite tweet |number=572906040494194688 |user=chy_leigh |title=@DavidHarewood: Just another day at the office.#Supergirl "A pleasure meeting my boss yesterday at the #tableread!! |author-link=Chyler Leigh |date=March 3, 2015 |access-date=March 12, 2015 |last=Leigh |first=Chyler}}</ref> She also meets and befriends police detective Maggie Sawyer and begins to develop feelings for her, forcing Alex to confront her sexuality. Jordan Mazarati and Olivia Nikkanen portray a young Alex.<ref name="gerding">{{Cite web |last=Gerding |first=Stephen |date=August 26, 2015 |title=Official Supergirl Pilot Synopsis Lands Online |url=https://www.cbr.com/official-supergirl-pilot-synopsis-lands-online/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150924140257/http://www.comicbookresources.com/article/official-supergirl-pilot-synopsis-lands-online |archive-date=September 24, 2015 |access-date=September 20, 2015 |website=Comic Book Resources}}</ref><ref name="YoungActors" /> 
* [[Jeremy Jordan (actor, born 1984)|Jeremy Jordan]] as [[Toyman|Winslow "Winn" Schott Jr. / Toyman]] (seasons 1–3; guest: seasons 5–6): A tech expert who worked alongside Kara at CatCo, he is Kara's best friend and serves as one of her allies, helping her develop her costume and aiding her in her adventures. Winn has unrequited feelings for Kara and is a rival with James for her affection.
* [[David Harewood]] as [[Martian Manhunter|J'onn J'onzz / Martian Manhunter]]: The head of the DEO who takes [[Hank Henshaw]]'s likeness after Henshaw is killed in Peru while hunting J'onn. J'onn takes Henshaw's likeness to reform the DEO from within as well as to watch over Alex and Kara.<ref name="SupportingCast" /><ref name="LeighHarewoodKreisberg" /> The evolution of Henshaw was discussed during the filming of the pilot, with the executive producers jokingly saying that Harewood would be a good actor to play the Martian Manhunter in a potential television series, to which [[DC Comics]]' [[Geoff Johns]] asked why it could not be done in ''Supergirl''. Harewood reflected that he had difficulty "find[ing] an angle to play Hank Henshaw" in the pilot, and became excited when he was told about the change to his character's backstory.<ref name="MMCBR">{{Cite web |last=Ratcliffe |first=Amy |date=December 7, 2015 |title="SUPERGIRL" EPS, HAREWOOD & LEIGH DISCUSS TONIGHT'S MAJOR REVEAL |url=https://www.cbr.com/supergirl-eps-harewood-leigh-discuss-tonights-major-reveal/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151210195959/http://www.comicbookresources.com/article/harewood-leigh-supergirl-eps-discuss-tonights-major-reveal |archive-date=December 10, 2015 |access-date=December 8, 2015 |website=Comic Book Resources}}</ref> Harewood also recurred in the series as the real Hank Henshaw, who became [[Cyborg Superman]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=November 21, 2016 |title=Supergirl sneak peek: Cyborg Superman revealed! |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/11/21/supergirl-cyborg-superman-hank-henshaw |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161122014921/http://www.ew.com/article/2016/11/21/supergirl-cyborg-superman-hank-henshaw |archive-date=November 22, 2016 |access-date=November 22, 2016}}</ref>
